-- title:
--   Special fibre points specialise from ξ_∞ or ξ₀
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M\neq 0$ together with a subgroup $H\leq(\mathbb Z/M)^\times$, and assume $p\mid M$, $p^2\nmid M$, and that every unit of $\mathbb Z/M$ whose image under reduction to $(\mathbb Z/(M/p))^\times$ is trivial lies in $H$; assume also that the Laurent series $\mathtt{jqModC}\ \mathbb Q=q^{-1}\cdot(\text{the integral power series }\mathtt{jNum})$ lies in the intermediate field $\mathtt{qExpFunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb Q\ \top$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of the Deligne–Rapoport property bundle `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for the two-chart integral model $X$ of level $\mathtt{ΓM}\ M\ H$ over the base ring $R\,p$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho\colon R\,p\to A$ be a ring map compatible with the structure map $R\,p\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $O$ be a local ring whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, $\rho_O\colon R\,p\to O$ a ring map, and $\mathrm{to}\kappa\colon O\to\kappa_A$ a ring map with $\mathrm{to}\kappa\circ\rho_O$ equal to the residue map composed with $\rho$. Write $X_O$ for the fibre product of the structure morphism of $X$ with $\operatorname{Spec}\rho_O$. Then for every point $y$ of $X_O$ whose image under $X_O\to\operatorname{Spec}O$ does not lie in the basic open set $\{p\neq 0\}$, at least one of the two distinguished points $\mathfrak X.\xi_\infty$, $\mathfrak X.\xi_0$ of $X_O$ attached to the data $(A,\rho,\rho_O,\mathrm{to}\kappa)$ specialises to $y$.
--
--   The statement says that the special fibre of the $O$-model $X_O$ of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ is the union of the closures of the two points $\xi_\infty$ and $\xi_0$, the generic points of the two parts of the geometric special fibre. It is used in the construction of oriented étale crossing charts at the supersingular points, via [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.forall_exists_orientedEtaleCrossingChart).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_bcMap_genericPoint_specializes_or.lean

